       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, or arrhythmias. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose for depression or anxiety.\n- **25 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a lower starting dose for panic disorder, PTSD, or sensitive patients.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is what you intend, for example as part of a specific protocol, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
