       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You confirmed the dose, but you didn't give a clinical reason for it. 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum, and I can't find a legitimate indication for it. The risk of serious harm is high, and an order that reaches the chart could be dispensed and given.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If the dose was a typo or misunderstanding,** give me the intended dose (for example 100 mg or 50 mg daily) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you think this dose is intentional,** discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. They can enter or verify it through the proper override process. I can then enter it with a note documenting the rationale and approval.\n- **If the patient has taken a large amount of sertraline,** that is an overdose. It needs urgent evaluation and a call to poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not a new order.\n\nI'm glad to help with any of these."
